[en.IDEA_C02_HOTLINE_HOOVES_PROJECT_018_DONE]
Political Psychology Survey: A Quantitative Analysis of the Impact of Propaganda Cases on Government Support Rate

[en.IDEA_C02_HOTLINE_HOOVES_PROJECT_018_DONE_desc]
Authors: Dr. Hooves, Mare, et al.
Abstract:
In this groundbreaking study, Dr. Hooves and Mare, along with their esteemed colleagues, delve into the fascinating world of political psychology. By harnessing the power of data collected during Mare’s tenure as the Mayor of Ponyville, the authors illuminate the intricate relationship between propaganda and public opinion. Through an innovative survey methodology, they measure the effectiveness of various propaganda techniques employed by the government in shaping the minds of the pony populace...

[zh.IDEA_C02_HOTLINE_HOOVES_PROJECT_018_DONE]
政治心理学综述——宣传事例对政府支持率影响的量化分析

[zh.IDEA_C02_HOTLINE_HOOVES_PROJECT_018_DONE_desc]
作者：蹄博士、梅耶等
摘要：
在这篇具有开创性的研究中，蹄博士和梅耶与他们的尊敬同事们一起，深入探讨了政治心理学的有趣世界。通过利用梅耶担任小马谷市长期间收集的数据，作者们阐明了政府宣传与公众舆论之间错综复杂的关系。通过创新的调查方法，他们衡量了政府采用的各种宣传技术在塑造小马族群思想方面的有效性...
